From: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] watchdog: mtk_wdt: read the DT mode properties before mtk_wdt_init()

mtk_wdt_probe() parses mediatek,disable-extrst and mediatek,reset-by-toprgu
at the very end, long after mtk_wdt_init() has run. init() is where a
watchdog left running by the bootloader is adopted, and what to do with the
inherited WDT_MODE depends on exactly those two properties — so as written
they could not influence that decision even in principle.

No functional change on its own: mtk_wdt_init() does not consult them yet.
The next patch makes it do so, and this ordering is its precondition.

Signed-off-by: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
@@ -390,6 +390,18 @@
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev, mtk_wdt);
 
+	/*
+	 * Read the mode properties before mtk_wdt_init(), not after. init()
+	 * decides what to do with a watchdog the bootloader left running, and
+	 * that decision depends on both of these — but they were parsed at the
+	 * very end of probe, so they could not influence it even in principle.
+	 */
+	mtk_wdt->disable_wdt_extrst =
+		of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "mediatek,disable-extrst");
+
+	mtk_wdt->reset_by_toprgu =
+		of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "mediatek,reset-by-toprgu");
+
 	mtk_wdt_init(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev);
 
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev);
@@ -408,12 +420,6 @@
 			return err;
 	}
 
-	mtk_wdt->disable_wdt_extrst =
-		of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "mediatek,disable-extrst");
-
-	mtk_wdt->reset_by_toprgu =
-		of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "mediatek,reset-by-toprgu");
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
